  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The federal market for Engineering Services (NAICS 541330) shows $31.7B in contract obligations for FY2026 to date, with totals for the year partial. Award count is 17,868 and average award size is $1.8M. Obligations are down 38.7% year over year compared with prior full fiscal years. Recent annual totals show FY21 at $39.6B, FY22 at $41.6B, FY23 at $47.8B, FY24 at $52.5B, and FY25 at $51.7B, putting the current-year pace below the last several full years. The Department of Defense accounts for the bulk of spending at $23.9B, followed by the General Services Administration at $3.4B and the Department of Transportation at $1.4B. Large vendors dominate the dollar totals: ELECTRIC BOAT CORPORATION leads with $6.8B, and BOOZ ALLEN HAMILTON INC is next at $1B. These figures reflect obligated contract dollars to date in FY2026 and are not full-year totals.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How big is the FY2026 to date market for NAICS 541330?",
        "body": "The market totals $31.7B in obligations for FY2026 to date. There are 17,868 awards and the average award size is $1.8M. Obligations are down 38.7% year over year, and current-year totals are partial rather than full fiscal year results."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the primary buyers and contractors in this market?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the primary buyer at $23.9B, followed by the General Services Administration at $3.4B and the Department of Transportation at $1.4B. ELECTRIC BOAT CORPORATION is the largest contractor at $6.8B, with BOOZ ALLEN HAMILTON INC at $1B and SCIENCE APPLICATIONS INTERNATIONAL CORPORATION at $896M among the top vendors."
      }
